# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Publication boundary — local-only, never tracked.
# Scrubbed from all history on 2026-08-12.
# These paths still exist on disk. Do not `git add -f` them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Manuscript sources, referee reports, and response letters.
# The published article is under journal copyright; referee material is
# confidential. This repository is code-only by design.
manuscript/

# Talk slides built on the paper.
slides/

# Pre-publication record: what was excluded from this repository and why,
# the history-scrub account, and the backup location. Local-only.
PUBLICATION_CHECKLIST.md

# Submission-process and internal-audit notes.
writing_comments.md
docs/

# Manuscript-support tooling: the LaTeX revision toolkit, its revision-artifact
# skeletons, and the test file that exercises them. Reusable for a future paper,
# but unrelated to the simulation code this repository publishes.
scripts/
templates/
tests/test_revision_tooling.py
LP_TEX_REF.md
PAPER_WRITING_SKILL.md

# Editor config (conda + latex-workshop build-on-save; personal tooling).
.vscode/

# Agent tooling config (local absolute paths, personal workflow record).
.claude/

# Mathematical reference notes and independent verification scripts.
# Untracked on 2026-08-13 — unlike the paths above, this one was NOT scrubbed
# from history; it remains visible in commits up to 88350e5.
analytics/

# Working-material notebooks that depend on the local-only analytics/ tree:
# an "options considered" record and an earlier snapshot of the _final
# notebook, plus the generators that built them. proof_of_concept_figures_final
# stays tracked — results/MANIFEST.md names it as the provenance for the
# paper's §2.2 figure.
notebooks/proof_of_concept_figures_aggregate.ipynb
notebooks/proof_of_concept_figures_backup.ipynb
notebooks/_tools/

